spec sk12-read-skew-lpg: 2 sessions, 35 permutations
# SK12 through the lpg API, extended to two keys (read skew, A5A). s1 reads x, then
# y, then x again inside one transaction; s2 moves 10 from x to y and commits. s1's
# two reads of x must agree and x + y must be 100 in every interleaving (F1). This
# spec is the negative control's target: a per-key snapshot breaks both.

starting permutation: s1x s1y s1x2 s1c s2dx s2cy s2c
step s1x: lpg: read x.bal
x.bal
-----
50   
(1 row)
step s1y: lpg: read y.bal
y.bal
-----
50   
(1 row)
step s1x2: lpg: read x.bal
x.bal
-----
50   
(1 row)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2dx: lpg: SetNodeProperty(x, bal, bal + -10)
step s2cy: lpg: SetNodeProperty(y, bal, bal + 10)
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
final final: MATCH (a:Account) RETURN sum(a.bal) AS total
total
-----
100  
(1 row)

